{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "28", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "01", "M": "51", "S": "44"}}, "news": [{"title": "Flex operators lease 1.91 lakh seats across top eight cities in H1 2026: Cushman & Wakefield", "para": "Flexible workspace operators leased 1,91,306 seats across India\u2019s top eight cities in H1 2026, up 68.4% year-on-year, according to Cushman & Wakefield. The segment recorded 8.4 million sq ft of gross leasing volume during the period, accounting for nearly 20% of total office leasing.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/commercial/flex-operators-lease-1-91-lakh-seats-across-top-eight-cities-in-h1-2026-cushman-wakefield/133581133?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-182388/133581133.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "commercial"}, {"title": "DTCP to intensify encroachment crackdown in compliance with HC, SC directives in Gurugram", "para": "The Gurgaon administration is intensifying its efforts to eliminate illegal constructions and encroachments. Town planner Amit Madholia highlighted that these actions are in line with court orders and prioritize public interest. The crackdown focuses on removing obstacles from public land and unauthorized building projects, with particular attention to stilt parking misuse. Residents are encouraged to report any violations and refrain from unlawful construction practices.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/dtcp-to-intensify-encroachment-crackdown-in-compliance-with-hc-sc-directives-in-gurugram/133581084?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-145046/133581084.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Patna civic body approves freehold conversion of 3,631 leasehold properties", "para": "The Patna Municipal Corporation has officially sanctioned the transition of 3,631 leasehold properties to freehold status. This initiative seeks to enhance transparency regarding property ownership and transactions. Original allottees will incur a conversion fee of ten percent based on market value, while second allottees face a twelve percent charge. The council also deliberated on addressing non-residential behaviors in residential areas.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/patna-civic-body-approves-freehold-conversion-of-3631-leasehold-properties/133581038?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-190014/133581038.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}